    "promptingNotes": "Reads natural language: write full, specific sentences, subject first, then setting, lighting, composition and style. Long, detailed prompts work well; tag lists and quality tags such as \"masterpiece, best quality\" add little. Put any text to render in the image in quotes. The seeded defaults are the Dev checkpoint's — 28 steps, no CFG, flow shift 1. The full checkpoint wants 50 steps at CFG 5 with flow shift 3. It was trained around 2048x2048 (2048x2048, 2304x1728, 2560x1440, 2496x1664, 3104x1312, 2304x1792 and their portraits); at 1024 it loses detail. Sides are multiples of 32. One file holds the whole model: no separate VAE or text encoder, only its tokenizer.json. On the drift runner the Dev checkpoint samples as the vendor's does (its distilled timesteps, fresh noise each step); sd-cpp runs plain Euler, which leaves the Dev images looking unfinished.",
