    "promptingNotes": "Reads natural language through Qwen3-VL-8B: write full, specific sentences, subject first, then setting, lighting, composition and style. Long, detailed prompts work well; tag lists and quality tags such as \"masterpiece, best quality\" add little. Put any text to render in the image in quotes — it is especially strong at text, Chinese included. Unlike Qwen Image, it steers on real classifier-free guidance rather than an embedded guidance value: CFG 6 with euler is the vendor's example, and the negative prompt does have an effect. The same checkpoint edits: attach one or more reference images and say in plain words what to change (\"change 'qwen2.1.cpp' to 'sd.cpp'\"), naming what must stay as it is. Editing reads the references through the text encoder, so it needs the Qwen3-VL-8B vision projector in the optional slot; generating from a prompt alone does not.",
